{%- comment -%}
  Hidden option-group properties for a Simple Bundles & Kits bundle parent.

  A bundle of three DIFFERENT variants (the scent trio) expands into three order
  lines on its own, because each component is a distinct variant. A bundle of
  three of the SAME variant does not: Shopify merges cart lines that share a
  variant AND identical properties, so the wipes 3-pack arrived at the warehouse
  as one line of quantity 3. The 3PL needs to see three products to pack.

  The fix is to configure the bundle in the app with one option group per unit.
  Distinct group names mean distinct properties per component, so nothing merges.
  The app only expands when those properties arrive with the add to cart, and
  the 3-pack sells through a plain product form that submits nothing but `id`,
  so we attach them here.

  Names must match the app's configuration character for character, so they live
  in theme settings rather than being hardcoded — see the "Bundle line
  properties" group in theme settings.

  @param {object} product - product whose add-to-cart form is being rendered
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bundle_product = settings.bundle_props_product
  assign group_names = settings.bundle_props_names
  assign group_value = settings.bundle_props_value
-%}

{%- if bundle_product != blank and group_names != blank and group_value != blank -%}
  {%- if product.id == bundle_product.id -%}
    {%- assign names = group_names | split: ',' -%}
    {%- assign summary = '' -%}
    {%- for name in names -%}
      {%- assign group_name = name | strip -%}
      {%- if group_name != blank -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="properties[{{ group_name | escape }}]" value="{{ group_value | escape }}">
        {%- if summary == blank -%}
          {%- assign summary = group_value -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign summary = summary | append: ' <> ' | append: group_value -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The app's own widget pairs the groups with a "_bundle_selection" summary,
      and both custom bundle sections replicate it for that reason. The widget
      only runs on the product page, so without this an add from a collection
      card or the sidecart upsell would reach the app missing a property its
      own adds always carry.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if summary != blank -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="properties[_bundle_selection]" value="{{ summary | escape }}">
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
